# ===== F3: THE REFUSAL ANSWERED A QUESTION THAT NEEDED NO AUTHORITY ========
#
# A failed-recoverable origin, a valid request shape, and an action this record
# never offers. Whether that action is valid is decidable from the record alone.
# Under the injection the completeness refusal runs first, so an UNRELATED
# session file with a line torn in its middle turns a malformed request into a
# retryable 503 — and repairing that file silently turns the same request into
# the actionable 400. A caller cannot tell a typo from a transient failure, and
# retrying is exactly the wrong response to a typo.
#
# The fix is an ordering change and not a relaxation: the same unreadable file
# still answers 503 to a WELL-FORMED request, because that request reaches the
# branch that mints authority. `an_invalid_action_answers_400_even_while_the_
# enumeration_is_unresolved` asserts both directions, so an injection that
# merely deleted the refusal would fail it too.
contains: an action this record never offers is decidable without any authority, so an unreadable sibling file must not turn it into a retryable 503
contains: left: 503
contains: right: 400

# ===== F2: ONE POST, TWO FULL PASSES OVER THE SAME FILES ===================
#
# `post_run_recover` calls `recovery_status_inner` to classify the run it was
# handed, and that function enumerated the project to do it. The handler then
# discarded that authority and built another for the claim decision. Against the
# round-three measurement of 1.15 GiB / 340 ms per pass, one POST paid roughly
# two full passes before any action executed — and the second was invisible to
# `ProjectOriginAuthority::cost()`, so it never appeared in the inventory
# metrics at all.
#
# `one_authority_serves_every_claim_in_a_project` cannot see this: it hands both
# callers the SAME authority object and counts through it. The count here lives
# outside both objects, in `recovery_claim::origin_enumeration_passes`.
contains: one recover decision must enumerate the project's session files ONCE
contains: left: 2
contains: right: 1
contains: test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 2 failed
